Project Context: Real-Time Chess Engine (v. Final)
Current Status:
I am currently working on the Graphical Interface (GUI) integration using OpenCV (cv2). The game engine logic (domain and services) is already implemented and supports:

Rules: Standard movement, pawn special rules (2-step start, promotion, diagonal capture), and king capture (game over).

Real-time Mechanics: Moves take time, jumping mechanics (1000ms), mid-air capture logic, and movement conflicts.

Project Structure:

core/: Domain models (Board, Pieces), Services (GameService), and Config.

interfaces/graphics/: BoardRenderer (using cv2 and a custom Img wrapper), ui_main.py (main loop), and ui_events.py (InputController).

interfaces/shared/: Helper functions like pixel_to_cell / cell_to_pixel.

Current Task:
I am actively implementing the GUI. I have successfully integrated cv2.setMouseCallback to handle inputs via InputController. I am currently debugging the rendering logic:

Aligning sprites correctly in the grid (using cell_to_pixel).

Fixing alpha-channel transparency (rendering pieces without white backgrounds).

Key Constraint: I am not using game libraries like Pygame. All rendering is done via OpenCV imshow and manual canvas manipulation using the Img class.